Mosquitto works based on a subscriber and publisher model

The subscriber listens for the publisher's message and takes in basic strings as commands 
Usage of Node-RED allows for control of a general-purpose input/outpit (GPIO) pin in response to MQTT message publications.

###### COMMANDS ######

--- SUBSCRIBER INIT ---
mosquitto_sub -d -t chimera

--- PUBLISHER INIT ---
mosquitto_pub -d -t chimera -m "saying hello"



One example usage would be to automate a schedule for turning off your living room lights 
